{"availability":"available","full":"kyhsa93/toddler-milestone-checklist","name":"toddler-milestone-checklist","description":"Personal, installable PWA for tracking developmental milestones from 2 to 36 months across four domains, plus a height/weight growth log from birth. Korean and English. Not a diagnostic tool.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-08T18:15:37Z","updated":"2026-10-10T23:33:17Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kyhsa93.github.io/toddler-milestone-checklist/","topics":["child-development","developmental-milestones","growth-chart","javascript","offline-first","pwa"],"demo":"https://kyhsa93.github.io/toddler-milestone-checklist/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.598Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.598Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.598Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.598Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A personal, installable PWA for tracking developmental milestones from 2 to 36 months, plus a simple height/weight growth log (which covers birth onward). Available in Korean and English (toggle in the top-right corner); UI defaults to Korean until a language is chosen, and the choice is remembered on the device.","The checklist covers four domains — social/emotional, language/communication, cognitive, and physical/motor — across all ten age bands CDC publishes for this range (2, 4, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 24, 30, 36 months). It's not autism-specific: this is CDC's own general developmental surveillance approach for spotting possible delay in any of the four domains, and the result breaks down \"not yet\" counts per domain for exactly that reason."],"features":["Age lock: entering the child's birthdate automatically locks age bands they haven't reached yet, so the result isn't skewed by milestones they can't be expected to show. Age is computed from the birthdate on every…","Regression check: a standalone question — has the child lost a skill they used to have? — independent of the age-band checklist, since CDC/AAP guidance treats regression as worth a pediatrician visit on its own,…","Print summary: the result card has a button to print a clean summary — meant to be brought to a pediatrician visit, not just looked at once.","Share: one footer button, defaults to sharing only the app's name, description, and URL. If you have a checked result, it asks first whether to include it — only appends it on an explicit \"yes.\" It never reads growth…","Growth log with percentiles: a date/height/weight log with a trend chart, plus a height/weight percentile per entry (requires entering the child's birthdate and sex). Uses the WHO Child Growth Standards under 24 months…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kyhsa93/toddler-milestone-checklist/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"448a6086ff146089bdd35c89d7d7e840f40320510d331f633a12b8e1c7611f78","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.719Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.719Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A personal, installable PWA for tracking developmental milestones from 2 to 36 months, plus a simple height/weight growth log (which covers birth onward). Available in Korean and English (toggle in the top-right corner); UI defaults to Korean until a language is chosen, and the choice is remembered on the device.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kyhsa93/toddler-milestone-checklist/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Run node --test \"test/.test.mjs\" to exercise the collector against a stub server; it needs no API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kyhsa93/toddler-milestone-checklist/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"448a6086ff146089bdd35c89d7d7e840f40320510d331f633a12b8e1c7611f78","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kyhsa93/toddler-milestone-checklist/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.719Z"},"o